<worksheet >
    <title>DC-1 Partial Derivatives</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to correctly label and state all six partial derivatives. 
      To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to correctly label and state at least four of the six partial derivatives.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <p>Find all first-order and second-order partial derivatives of the function <m>f(x,y) = \frac{e^{2x}}{y^3+1}</m>.</p>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>